WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.358
With Rosa’s file complete, the underwriter places her in a class.

00:00:04.358 --> 00:00:09.112
Preferred applicants have better-than-average health and habits and pay the lowest rate.

00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:13.470
Standard applicants match the pricing assumptions and pay the base rate.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:17.431
Substandard applicants present higher risk and are accepted with a

00:00:17.431 --> 00:00:20.997
higher premium, a benefit limitation or an exclusion rider.

00:00:20.997 --> 00:00:24.166
Declined applicants are not accepted at any price.

00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:28.128
For disability income, Rosa’s electrical trade may place her in

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:32.090
a riskier occupational class even if her health is excellent.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:37.240
Classification is lawful when it rests on sound actuarial differences in expected claims.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.904
An underwriter who finds Rosa’s back injury has choices short of declining.

00:00:41.904 --> 00:00:45.402
A rated premium charges more for the added risk.

00:00:45.402 --> 00:00:50.843
An exclusion rider removes claims caused by the back condition while covering everything else.

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:55.507
A modified benefit shortens the benefit period or lengthens the elimination period.

00:00:55.507 --> 00:00:59.394
Each tool lets the insurer offer something rather than nothing.

00:00:59.394 --> 00:01:02.503
Rosa may accept the counteroffer or shop elsewhere.

00:01:02.503 --> 00:01:07.556
Theo must explain exactly what an exclusion rider removes, because an insured who

00:01:07.556 --> 00:01:12.220
later files a back claim will be told it is not covered.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:16.835
Unfair discrimination means treating people in the same actuarial class differently,

00:01:16.835 --> 00:01:21.450
or using a characteristic that has no legitimate relation to risk.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:26.065
Charging two 41-year-old electricians with identical health different rates because of

00:01:26.065 --> 00:01:30.681
race, religion or national origin is unfair discrimination and is prohibited.

00:01:30.681 --> 00:01:36.135
So is refusing coverage on a basis the law has removed from underwriting.

00:01:36.135 --> 00:01:40.750
Lawful classification uses age, health, occupation and habits supported by data.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:45.785
The test is whether the distinction reflects a real difference in expected

00:01:45.785 --> 00:01:50.400
claims and whether the law permits that factor to be used.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.252
Maryland forbids insurers from using the fact that a person is

00:01:54.252 --> 00:01:57.755
or has been a victim of domestic violence against them.

00:01:57.755 --> 00:02:01.257
An insurer may not deny, cancel, refuse to renew, limit

00:02:01.257 --> 00:02:04.759
or price coverage because the applicant was abused, and may

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:07.911
not treat the abuse itself as a pre-existing condition.

00:02:07.911 --> 00:02:10.713
If Elena’s coworker is injured by a partner,

00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:13.514
her injuries are a claim like any other.

00:02:13.514 --> 00:02:18.067
Insurers may still consider a medical condition on its own actuarial terms, but

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:22.620
not the abuse that caused it or the status of being a victim.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.525
Maryland and federal law protect genetic information.

00:02:25.525 --> 00:02:31.335
An insurer offering health coverage may not request or require a genetic test, use

00:02:31.335 --> 00:02:37.145
genetic test results or family history of genetic conditions to deny or price coverage,

00:02:37.145 --> 00:02:42.955
or treat a genetic predisposition as a pre-existing condition when no disease has appeared.

00:02:42.955 --> 00:02:47.520
If Marcus carries a gene associated with a condition he does

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.670
not have, a medical insurer may not use that fact.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.650
The protections for life, disability and long-term care insurance are narrower, so

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:01.630
read the question for the type of coverage before applying the rule.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.900
Underwriting is a sorting process bounded by law.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:08.987
It starts with the application and producer’s report, adds medical

00:03:08.987 --> 00:03:13.075
and lifestyle information with the applicant’s notice and consent, checks

00:03:13.075 --> 00:03:17.162
for consistency and ends in a class and an offer.

00:03:17.162 --> 00:03:22.067
Along the way the insurer may not use a forbidden factor, may

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:26.972
not treat identical risks differently and must give the Fair Credit Reporting

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:31.059
Act and adverse underwriting notices when it declines or rates.

00:03:31.059 --> 00:03:35.964
Theo’s role is to gather complete and honest information, explain any counteroffer

00:03:35.964 --> 00:03:40.460
plainly and never promise an outcome the underwriter has not reached.
